  'adv.volume1.b': 'The range for your training load is {low} to {high}, with {aim} as the aim. One more phase of the plan covers the rest.',
  'adv.volume0.t': '{a}: at or above the aim for your training load',
  'adv.volume0.b': 'Range {low} to {high}. Hold it; from here regularity is worth more than extra minutes.',
  'adv.targetOver.t': 'Your target of {target} sits above the range for this training load',
  'adv.targetOver.b': 'The range tops out at {high}. A target you rarely reach makes the gap look worse than it is: bring it inside the range, or pick a heavier training load below if that fits your weeks better.',
  'adv.targetUnder.t': 'Your target of {target} sits below the range for this training load',
  'adv.targetUnder.b': 'The range starts at {low}. Consider raising the target.',
  'adv.onset1.t': 'You fall asleep around {on}, after midnight on {late} of {n} nights',
  'adv.onset1.b': 'With a wake time near {off}, every minute past midnight comes straight out of the night, and out of its last hours, the ones richest in REM sleep. Earlier lights-out is the only lever that adds sleep without moving your mornings.',
  'adv.onset0.t': 'You fall asleep around {on}',
  'adv.onset0.b': 'Before midnight on most nights. No hour is magic in itself; what counts is that it leaves room for a full night before {off}.',
  'adv.jetlag1.t': 'Days off run {jl} later than workdays',
  'adv.jetlag1.b': 'Mid-sleep sits at {mw} before workdays and {mf} on days off. That shift acts like a small jet lag every week and makes Sunday night harder. Keeping the wake time within an hour on days off is the fix.',
  'adv.jetlagNeg.t': 'Workdays run {jl} later than days off',
  'adv.jetlagNeg.b': 'Mid-sleep sits at {mw} before workdays and {mf} on days off. The late evenings are the workday ones, so that is where to act.',
  'adv.jetlag0.t': 'Workdays and days off line up',
  'adv.jetlag0.b': 'Mid-sleep at {mw} before workdays and {mf} on days off: less than half an hour apart.',
  'adv.sri1.t': 'Regularity: {v} out of 100',
  'adv.sri1.b': 'Half of the adults in the reference study score between {q1} and {q3}, with {q2} in the middle. Wake times that stay close from one day to the next move this number faster than anything else.',
